Relevant columns & how they can be used  

• FINANCE__ECONOMICS.CYBERSYN.FINANCIAL_BRANCH_ENTITIES  
  – "CATEGORY": filter to 'Branch' so only branch‑level entities are counted.  
  – "ID_COUNTRY": keep rows where value = 'country/USA'.  
  – "STATE_ABBREVIATION": two‑letter state code for grouping.  
  – "ID_STATE": fips‑style geoId for a state (optional if fuller name needed).  
  – "START_DATE": branch opening date – must be ≤ the reference date to be active.  
  – "END_DATE": closing date – NULL or ≥ the reference date to be active.  
  – "IS_ACTIVE": quick check of current status (not used in point‑in‑time logic).  
  – "ID_RSSD": unique identifier of the branch – use COUNT(DISTINCT …) when aggregating.

• FINANCE__ECONOMICS.CYBERSYN.GEOGRAPHY_INDEX (optional)  
  – "GEO_ID": join to "ID_STATE".  
  – "GEO_NAME": full state name if you need readable labels.  

Conditions that will appear in the final query  

```
"START_DATE" <= {reference_date}
AND ("END_DATE" IS NULL OR "END_DATE" >= {reference_date})
AND "CATEGORY" = 'Branch'
AND "ID_COUNTRY" = 'country/USA'
```

